?" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/f5/f52592db0fee86e26318d6d2de9d7f685f1fb9f5d416628a04878857f1c54b54.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/76/76f0da764caf0237a2d30d32d593886d8df6c348368fe889f7447be781b6faf1.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/97/9778abd955cdc9b705800eba8f3d0d635af1c6a5fd5724583bdb32a943c6d44f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110675 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9ef4e321-841e-5933-b5e4-ff7dab6c5275" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Collinear Points on a Grid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe09bc4-31c7-568f-be87-02c28b0907ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530929} {:answer/id #uuid "4160685f-7ffd-5ade-9845-5db543cb5598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531003} {:answer/id #uuid "88414189-b1f0-5218-8c18-851c2eff974f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531162} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e424dc-7e89-5bd6-b6e8-84d2d9dea85f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531271} {:answer/id #uuid "ec66f155-3fe5-5781-8a8a-8f6d97fb5483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/i